
# ⚙️ How It Works

The Weather Monitoring Station works by measuring the surrounding temperature and humidity using a DHT11 sensor. The Arduino Uno reads this information and shows it on a 16×2 I2C LCD display.

### Step 1 – Power On
When the Arduino Uno is powered through the USB cable, it starts the program and initializes the DHT11 sensor and the LCD display.

### Step 2 – Reading Sensor Data
The DHT11 sensor measures the temperature and humidity of the surrounding environment. It sends this data to the Arduino through its data pin.

### Step 3 – Processing the Data
The Arduino receives the sensor values and processes them using the program uploaded to the board.

### Step 4 – Displaying the Values
The processed temperature and humidity values are displayed on the 16×2 I2C LCD. The display updates automatically after a short delay.

### Step 5 – Continuous Monitoring
The Arduino keeps reading the sensor repeatedly in a loop. This allows the display to show the latest temperature and humidity values continuously while the system is powered on.

---

## 📌 Working Summary

- Power ON the Arduino.
- Initialize the DHT11 sensor and LCD.
- Read temperature and humidity from the sensor.
- Process the sensor data.
- Display the values on the LCD.
- Repeat the process continuously.